      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Some academics do bring up cultural differences, suggesting that the way certain groups are socialized or taught might not align perfectly with the specific cultural norms embedded in standardized tests. Others point to potential cognitive or processing differences, though these claims are often heavily debated and criticized. Ultimately, while some look for subtle cultural or innate factors, the majority of critical research points back to the persistent, unmeasured effects of historical and ongoing systemic inequality.",
